	{page:WordSection1;}Edfinity is an
education technology platform supported by the National Science Foundation and
used at over 400 institutions, including some of the largest public university
systems in the country. We are a pioneer in AI-powered mathematics education.
Our platform applies current AI to the genuinely hard problem of evaluating
student reasoning and proof-style explanations, not just checking final
answers. We are reshaping how undergraduate mathematics and statistics are
taught and assessed, and we are growing quickly.


We are looking
for current faculty members at 4-year colleges and universities to lead
academic outreach and engagement on a part-time basis (10–20 hours per week).
This is a peer-facing role designed to fit alongside a full faculty life: you
keep teaching, researching, and serving your department, while spending a
modest number of flexible hours helping fellow mathematicians understand what
AI genuinely can and cannot do in the classroom.


The best person
to talk with mathematics faculty about teaching in an AI age is someone who is
still standing at the front of a classroom. Your standing among peers, your
teaching practice, and your ability to articulate the effective and ethical use
of AI will be central to the role.


















