or teaching-stream) at a 4-year college or university, with a PhD in
mathematics or statistics


•    
Active teaching experience and a real feel for
undergraduate mathematics education — experience with large-enrollment courses,
course coordination, or homework-system authoring (e.g., WeBWorK) is a plus


•    
Standing in the professional community — MAA section
activity, Project NExT, committee work, workshops — and genuine enjoyment in
meeting people and presenting


•    
Genuine curiosity about AI and how it is reshaping
mathematics education, and the ability to discuss it credibly, including its
limits, with faculty


•    
Strong communication skills across speaking and
writing, and comfort working independently in a remote, fast-moving environment


•    
Availability for occasional travel to conferences and
academic events, consistent with your academic calendar






