University of Utah, Department of Mathematics


Postdoctoral Positions in Pure and Applied Mathematics 



The Department of Mathematics at the University of Utah invites applications for one or more postdoctoral positions in pure and applied mathematics. These are 3-year, termed positions that involve research and teaching. Successful applicants might also receive additional opportunities through the Cecil Edmund Burgess and C. R. Wiley endowed Instructorships, as well as individual faculty research. Ideal applicants would align with our existing research strengths and be effective educators. Candidates are expected to have completed a Ph.D. in Mathematics or in a closely related field by July 1, 2027.

Applications must include: (1) a cover letter; (2) a curriculum vitae; (3) a list of publications; (4) a statement of research interests and plans; (5) a teaching statement; and (6) four or more letters of recommendation, at least one of which must address the candidate’s teaching record. Applicants are encouraged to mention in their cover letter the name(s) of faculty at the University of Utah whose research aligns with their own.

Applications must be completed through MathJobs at https://www.mathjobs.org/jobs/UofUtah/PD. Please see also our website at https://www.math.utah.edu/about/hiring-current.php for additional information regarding available positions.

Completed applications received before December 15, 2026, will receive full consideration. Review of applications may continue beyond these deadlines until the positions are filled. The position has an anticipated start date of July 1, 2027.
